@startuml 05-content-lifecycle
' Source of truth for docs/images/05-content-lifecycle.svg — regenerated by
' .github/workflows/render-diagrams.yml. Edit this file, never the SVG.
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam DefaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #F4F7FB
skinparam StateBorderColor #33475B
skinparam ArrowColor #33475B
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FBEFD5
skinparam NoteBorderColor #A9822C

state "DRAFT" as Draft
state "PUBLISHED" as Published

[*] --> Draft : createPost() / createWork()\n(lifecycleState defaults to DRAFT,\ndate/slug are set exactly once)

Draft --> Draft : autosave\n(3-minute debounce OR field blur;\nPUT — replaces the ENTIRE document,\nnever a patch)

Draft --> Published : Publish\n(explicit admin action:\nflush() → strict Zod validation\nof the DB row → lifecycleState=PUBLISHED,\npublishedAt set if not already)

Published --> Draft : Unpublish\n(explicit admin action)

Published --> Draft : a save stopped\nsatisfying the strict publish\nschema (an automatic\n"safety net", not a publish!)

Draft --> [*] : Delete
Published --> [*] : Delete

note right of Draft
  **Document blocks** (Document → Block[], order = array index):
  lead · heading(H2/H3) · paragraph · quote(+attribution) · note(info|
  warning|tip) · image · code(language+filename) · approachList · list
  (nested, ordered/unordered) · diagram(engine: mermaid|plantuml).

  **Parsing pasted markdown** (paste-handler.ts, a custom splitter that
  runs BEFORE handing the remainder to BlockNote):
  • ```lang ... ```              → a code block (or diagram, if lang is
                                    mermaid/plantuml)
  • consecutive "> " lines       → one quote block (markers stripped)
  • everything else              → editor.pasteMarkdown() from BlockNote:
                                    ## / ### → heading, **/*/`code`/links
                                    → inline formatting, -/*/1. → list
  The lead, note, image and approachList blocks can only be inserted via
  the slash menu — pasting markdown can't produce them, because none of
  them has an unambiguous plain-text equivalent.
end note

note left of Published
  publishedAt is set EXACTLY ONCE, on the first transition into PUBLISHED,
  and is never cleared by Unpublish — it answers "when was this last
  published," not "is this published right now" (that's lifecycleState's
  job).
end note

note bottom
  **There is no scheduled auto-publish in this project.** No scheduledAt
  field, no cron job, no background worker that would move a record from
  DRAFT to PUBLISHED on its own — none of that exists. The only automatic
  transition in this state machine actually points the other way:
  PUBLISHED → DRAFT, whenever a subsequent autosave stops satisfying the
  strict publish requirements (say, a required field got cleared out of an
  already-published draft). This is a deliberate architectural decision,
  not a forgotten feature: the only cron job that genuinely exists in this
  repository is the nightly pg_dump backup
  (.scripts/provision/11-pg-backup.sh), which has nothing to do with
  content publishing.
end note

@enduml
